ived 10% weighting in our comprehensive evaluation framework. We examined Portuguese bank transfers, regional payment support, and e-wallet compatibility. Customer support quality and trading flexibility comprised the remaining 25%.</p>\n\n<h2 style=\"color: #4250eb;\" id=\"prop-trading-info\">Prop Trading in Portugal: What You Need to Know</h2>\n\n<p>Prop trading operates legally throughout Portugal. CMVM (Comissao do Mercado de Valores Mobiliarios) does not require individual traders to obtain licenses for joining prop firms. These companies function as educational platforms using simulated trading accounts.</p>\n\n<p>Portuguese residents face no legal restrictions when participating in prop trading. You can verify identity using passports, driving licenses, or Cartao de Cidadao. Standard proof of address documents like utility bills are also accepted.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"color: #4250eb;\">Tax Considerations</h3>\n\n<p>Trading profits are taxed as self-employment income in Portugal. Tax rates range from 14.5% to 48% depending on your total income bracket. Additional social security contributions may apply through the Portuguese social insurance system.</p>\n\n<p>You must declare your trading income to Autoridade Tributaria. Consult a qualified Portuguese contabilista certificado for personalized tax guidance. Proper record-keeping is essential for annual tax returns.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"color: #4250eb;\">Payment Methods in Portugal</h3>\n\n<p>Portuguese traders use several payment methods with proprietary trading firms:</p>\n<ul>\n    <li><strong>Visa and Mastercard</strong> - Instant deposits accepted</li>\n    <li><strong>Cryptocurrency</strong> - Bitcoin, Ethereum, Solana, Ripple, and Doge supported</li>\n    <li><strong>Digital wallets</strong> like Skrill - Instant processing available</li>\n    <li><strong>Bank transfers</strong> - Process within 1-2 business days</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Traders Yard accepts multiple payment methods including crypto for faster proce